        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Yes, standard homeowners insurance policies in Utah typically cover hail damage. This includes damage to your home's roof, siding, windows, and other outdoor structures like fences or detached garages, as well as interior damage caused by hail leaks.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Policy Details"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Separate Deductibles: Many policies in storm-prone regions use a separate wind and hail deductible, which can be a flat dollar amount or a percentage of your total dwelling coverage.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cosmetic Exclusions: Some insurers exclude purely cosmetic dents on metal roofs or siding if the function of the material is not impaired.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Filing Guidance: You can review consumer guidelines or ask questions directly via the Utah Insurance Department regarding local claim rules."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want to check your potential costs, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is your policy's wind/hail deductible\n?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What part of your home was damaged?"
          }
        ]
      }
